.TH "OSTRYA\-LS" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-ls \- List the file paths of a commit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya ls [OPTIONS] [COMMIT] [PATH]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the file paths of a commit.
.PP
The command prints one line for each entry: the type and the permission bits, the uid, the gid, the size, and the path. A symlink adds \fB\% \-> <target>\fR\&. The type is \fB\%d\fR for a directory, \fB\%\-\fR for a regular file, and \fB\%l\fR for a symlink. A directory prints its own line, then its files, then its subdirectories, each in name order.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fICOMMIT\fR
The commit to list (a checksum or a ref). Required.
.TP
\fIPATH...\fR
The paths in the commit to list, in order.
.IP
With no PATH, the command lists the tree root. A leading \fB\%/\fR is optional. A PATH that names a file prints one line. A PATH that names nothing is an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dironly\fR
Print the line of each directory argument alone, without its entries.
.IP
This switch wins over \%\-R.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-recursive\fR
Print directories recursively.
.IP
The entries of each subdirectory follow its own line. Without this switch, the command prints one level of entries.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-checksum\fR
Print the checksum of each entry.
.IP
A file shows its content checksum. A directory shows its dirtree checksum and then its dirmeta checksum.
.TP
\fB\-X\fR, \fB\-\-xattrs\fR
Print the extended attributes of each entry.
.IP
The set prints after the checksums, in the GVariant text form between \fB\%{ \fR and \fB\% }\fR\&.
.TP
\fB\-\-nul\-filenames\-only\fR
Print only the paths, NUL separated.
.IP
Each path ends with a NUL byte, and the output has no newline. This switch wins over \%\-C and \%\-X.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
